# Compiled binaries always carry an extension, per CLAUDE.md's Build section:
# .bin on Linux and macOS, .exe on Windows. Both are here because a
# cross-compile follows the target rather than the host.
*.bin
*.exe

# Anything fetched that the module system does not manage lands here, unpacked,
# and is reproducible from the pins. See .guidelines/bootstrapping.md.
thirdparty/

# The working record: how this was planned, proved, reviewed and logged, and
# the conventions it was written to. Kept on disk, out of the repository.
.claude/
.doc/
.guidelines/
.poc/
CLAUDE.md
plan.md
review.md
revision.md
testing.md

# A WSL utility for deleting Windows Zone.Identifier sidecars. It lives here
# because that is where it is run from, not because it belongs to this project.
purge_zone_identifier.py

# Editor settings. Whoever works here chooses their own; a copy in the tree
# would make one person's choices everybody else's.
.vscode/

# Things that land in a working directory and belong to no project: a package
# downloaded to install something, an archive unpacked in place. One of these
# reached a commit on 2026-09-27 because a `git add -A` swept it up, and left
# again in the next commit. Naming them here is cheaper than remembering.
*.deb
*.rpm
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
